========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) 8.1.2 - MULTI-NODE CLUSTER TROUBLESHOOTING COMMANDS
========================================================================================================================

CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cluster Health         sudo pcs status                                 Check overall cluster, nodes, and resource status
Cluster Health         sudo crm_mon -1                                 Get a quick single-shot summary of active nodes
Cluster Health         sudo pcs status --full                          View absolute details including hidden attributes
Cluster Health         sudo corosync-cmapctl | grep members            Verify cluster members acknowledged by Corosync
Cluster Health         sudo systemctl status corosync                  Check underlying cluster sync heartbeat service
Cluster Health         sudo systemctl status pacemaker                 Check the cluster orchestrator service health

Node Management        sudo pcs node standby <node_name>               Place a specific node into maintenance standby
Node Management        sudo pcs node unstandby <node_name>             Bring a node back online to host active workloads
Node Management        sudo pcs cluster stop --all                     Stop the cluster manager services on all nodes
Node Management        sudo pcs cluster start --all                    Start the cluster manager services on all nodes
Node Management        sudo pcs cluster enable --all                   Enable auto-start on boot across all cluster nodes
Node Management        sudo pcs cluster disable --all                  Disable auto-start on boot across all cluster nodes

Resource & Stonith     sudo pcs resource status                        Display current placement/state of cluster resources
Resource & Stonith     sudo pcs resource cleanup <resource_id>         Clear error flags and force a retry on a resource
Resource & Stonith     sudo pcs stonith history                        Review historical fencing / STONITH events 
Resource & Stonith     sudo pcs stonith cleanup <fencing_id>           Reset a fencing tracking block after an event
Resource & Stonith     sudo tail -f /var/log/pacemaker/pacemaker.log   Stream live node election and resource fence events

Cluster Storage        sudo ceph status                                Review primary health status of Ceph storage pool
Cluster Storage        sudo ceph osd tree                              Map physical drive topologies and failure domains
Cluster Storage        sudo ceph health detail                         Expose hidden storage warnings or degraded PG lists
Cluster Storage        sudo dlm_tool ls                                List active Distributed Lock Manager lockspaces
Cluster Storage        sudo dlm_tool status                            Verify current DLM operating parameters for GFS2
Cluster Storage        mount | grep gfs2                               Verify active local mount points for GFS2 volumes
